modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","title":"finishRequest with no active request or no done file just closes the menu; no files are created or truncated."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","title":"open(payload) dispatches on mode: select/input open the dmenu flow, anything else opens the resolved route; close() cancels; refresh() reloads both JSONC files and returns ok; ping() returns ok."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-C8HX","title":"finishRequest with a null selection (Escape/cancel) creates only the done file, so the caller observes the cancel as an empty selection."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-CYB9","title":"Absent an exact id, a route equal to a declared alias (after lowercasing and underscore-to-dash normalization) resolves to the id of the item declaring the alias."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","title":"A row matches only when every query term appears in its name text (label, leaf id, aliases) or as a whole word in its description; invisible and disabled rows never match."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","title":"Full-line // comments and trailing commas are stripped before JSON parsing, so the authored JSONC parses to its declared entries."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","title":"finishRequest with a selection writes the value to the selection file and creates the done file, shell-quoted, and only then closes."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-MQ37","title":"The generated guard script holds exactly one if-line per declared when, checked, or disabled, each echoing <id>:<w|c|d>:<0|1>; items with no guard get none."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-PRNV","title":"An exact id match wins over every alias; app rows are never routable, so an installed app's keywords cannot shadow a menu route (htop ships Keywords=system)."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS","title":"The select payload carries mode=select, prompt, options, selectionFile, and doneFile, plus integer width/maxHeight only when given; options come from arguments or, with none and non-terminal stdin, from stdin lines."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-RGCV","title":"The prelude's omarchy-pkg-present/missing shadows agree with pacman -Q everywhere: provides resolution, version constraints deferred to pacman, and the no-argument case (present true of nothing, missing not)."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","title":"Scores tier exact label, whole-word app name, label prefix, label substring, name text, then description; menus and links promote by 2, apps demote by 5 within a tier; final order breaks ties by depth then declaration order."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-SNZG","title":"An unknown verb prints 'omarchy-menu: unknown verb' naming the verb to stderr and exits 2."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-T257","title":"toggle, summon, close, refresh, and ping each exec the matching omarchy-shell IPC call; toggle and summon pass the route as a JSON payload; help prints usage and exits 0."},{"changeStatus":"added","component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260925-XTGG","title":"A summon arriving while a select/input request is still active answers that prior request as cancelled (done file only, empty selection) before opening the new menu, so the caller polling the done file is never abandoned by a later summon."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","title":"omarchy-menu routes each verb (toggle/summon/close/refresh/ping) to the matching omarchy-shell IPC call so the menu opens, closes, refreshes, or answers ping."},{"changeStatus":"modified","component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","title":"A script-driven select/input prompt delivers the picked value to the caller (glyph stripped, subtext kept as the stable key); cancellation reaches the caller as no-selection."}],"linkedIssues":["#9057","omacom/omarchy#9057"],"sources":["changeRequest.body","changeRequest.linkedIssues","changeRequest.title","requirement:STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-50RE","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-C8HX","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-CYB9","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-MQ37","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-PRNV","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-RGCV","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-SNZG","requirement:SW-REQ-260922-T257","requirement:SW-REQ-260925-XTGG","requirement:SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","requirement:SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5"],"status":"declared","title":"Answer an abandoned menu request before starting the next one"},"nextDecision":{"disclosureIds":["policy_changed_unclassified","policy_weakened"],"kind":"human_judgement","question":"Should the 2 protection reductions this change makes be accepted under the prior approved policy?","reason":"protection_weakened"},"preservedBehaviour":{"requirements":[{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When every row is disabled the menu shows no cursor at all rather than parking one on a row Enter cannot run; the cursor returns the moment a row becomes selectable."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary","error_handling"],"relation":"code_changed","title":"Unparseable input (after stripping), non-object JSON, and non-object entries yield an empty or skipped item set; no exception escapes the parser."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A guard batch that exits nonzero or by signal is discarded whole (the last complete result set stays in effect), and an evaluation that stood aside runs once the process exits."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-46HY","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"An entry with action is an action, with target a link, otherwise a menu; an undeclared parent derives from the dotted id (or root); root's parent is empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Delete with the cursor on an app row opens an uninstall confirmation naming the app; confirming removes the app through the shared app library and closes the menu; cancelling closes the dialog and returns focus without removing anything. Non-app rows ignore the key."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When the rows do not fit, the list height ends mid-row: the clipped peek row tells the eye there is more below the fold, the height never lands exactly on a row boundary, and the card never exceeds 70 percent of panel height."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Drilling in pushes the previous menu on the navigation stack; Backspace/Left pops it, or falls back to the parent menu when the stack is empty; entering a menu clears the filter."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-EFNR","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"swapProviderRows drops exactly the rows carrying the re-run provider's providerMenu and appends the new batch, leaving static children and other providers' rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Applied guard results drive the view: a row hides when its when: is false, a static submenu or link hides when no descendant is visible, provider-backed menus stay visible, a checked:true or disabled:true row earns the check-mark label, and a disabled row dims and skips the cursor."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-N3RM","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When a route resolves to an action item with a non-empty action (e.g. an alias for a leaf), the action runs directly and no menu opens."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"A dmenu option may lead with a glyph TAB and trail a subtext TAB; the glyph is shown but never returned, and a subtext-bearing pick returns 'label TAB subtext' as the stable key."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Search lists current-menu matches before deeper (drilldown) matches, with a divider section exactly when both groups are non-empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-XW52","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"When a route resolves to a link item, the menu opens at the link's target."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"Cursor movement lands on the next selectable row in the direction of travel, wrapping at the list ends; disabled rows are stepped over."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z680","matchLevel":"file","relation":"code_changed","title":"mergeAppRows and swapProviderRows return fresh maps that drop orphan ids and the replaced batch, list a duplicated incoming id once, and never write into the maps they were handed."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"relation":"code_changed","title":"Activating a row runs its action, follows its link, or drills into its submenu; the cursor never rests on a disabled row; back navigation retraces the drill path."}],"total":16},"readiness":"blocked","readinessBasis":"introduced","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_p